const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is the easiest video calling app for seniors?',
    answer: 'FaceTime (for Apple iPhone and iPad users) is widely considered the easiest video calling app for seniors because it requires no separate account, no downloads, and works with one tap from the Contacts app. For seniors with non-Apple devices (Android phones, Amazon Fire tablets), Google Meet or WhatsApp Video are simple free alternatives that work across all device types.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is FaceTime and how does it work?',
    answer: 'FaceTime is a free video and audio calling app built into all Apple iPhones, iPads, and Mac computers. It uses your device\'s front-facing camera and microphone to show your live video image to another person while you see their video on your screen. FaceTime calls require a Wi-Fi or cellular data connection — calls are free as long as you have an internet connection.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need a Zoom account to join a Zoom video call?',
    answer: 'No. You can join a Zoom meeting as a guest without creating an account. When someone sends you a Zoom meeting link, tap or click the link and tap "Join as Guest" — you do not need to log in or create a password. The free Zoom app must be installed on your device the first time you join.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between Wi-Fi and cellular data for video calls?',
    answer: 'Wi-Fi is a wireless internet connection from your home router that allows video calls at no extra charge on most plans. Cellular data is your phone\'s internet connection through your carrier (AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile) when you are not connected to Wi-Fi. Video calls over cellular data consume significant data — approximately 600 MB per hour — which may result in extra charges if you have a limited data plan.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I make my phone or tablet screen larger and easier to read?',
    answer: 'On an iPhone or iPad: Go to Settings → Accessibility → Display & Text Size → Larger Text — then slide the text size all the way to the right for maximum size. On Android: Go to Settings → Accessibility → Font Size → and move the slider to Large or Extra Large. You can also go to Settings → Display → Screen Size for additional magnification.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is a telehealth visit and can I do it by video call?',
    answer: 'A telehealth visit is a medical appointment conducted by video call or phone, allowing you to consult with your doctor from home without traveling to a clinic. Most Medicare-covered telehealth visits use platforms like Zoom for Healthcare, Microsoft Teams, or your health system\'s patient portal app. Learn more about how telehealth works using our Telehealth How It Works explainer.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I make the video call buttons bigger on my smartphone?',
    answer: 'On iPhone: Go to Settings → Accessibility → AssistiveTouch and turn it On — this adds a large floating button to your screen for easier access to calls and functions. On Android: Go to Settings → Accessibility → Interaction Controls → Enable Large Navigation Buttons. Both options create larger touch targets for video call controls.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is it safe to video call family and friends on apps like Zoom or FaceTime?',
    answer: 'Yes. FaceTime uses end-to-end encryption, meaning only you and the person you are calling can see and hear each other — Apple cannot access your calls. Zoom uses AES-256 bit encryption for meeting content. Never share your Zoom meeting ID or password in response to an unexpected phone call or email — this is a common scammer tactic. Only join Zoom meetings from links sent directly by people you personally know.',
